# --- s051 Book I d.17 q.1
n("n812","s051-01","vtrum in mente sit ponere caritatem creatam inherentem nature beatificabili","la","source","This is almost verbatim Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 17 p. 1 q. 1–2 (‘Utrum necesse sit ponere caritatem creatam formaliter inhaerentem naturae beatificabili’). Gorris's *In hac distinctione simul mouet duas questiones* refers to the paired questions of Scotus's text.","to-verify")
n("n813","s051-01","in cordibus vestris","la","intertext","Rom 5:5. The Vulgate reads *in cordibus nostris*; A and B both have *vestris*.","verified")
n("n814","s051-01","Fructus spiritus sancti est caritas","la","intertext","Gal 5:22 (*fructus autem Spiritus est caritas*).","certain")
n("n815","s051-02","Henrici quodlibeto. 4. q. 10.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Quodl.* IV q. 10. The locus has not been checked against the Leuven edition.","to-verify")
n("n816","s051-02","virtus est que habentem perficit et opus eius bonum reddit","la","intertext","Aristotle, *Eth. Nic.* II 6, 1106a15–17.","certain")
n("n817","s051-02","sed est primo de celo","la","intertext","Gorris notes a philological error in ‘some books’: the definition *virtus est ultimum de potentia* is Aristotle, *De caelo* I 11 (281a), not *Ethics* II. The exact Bekker line has not been checked. The remark seems to concern copies of Scotus's text and is worth comparing with the Vatican edition's apparatus to *Ord.* I d. 17. B has the same sentence.","to-verify")
n("n818","s051-03","sed intensionem talem vel talem","la","textual","Thus A. B reads *intellectõꝫ* (= *intellectionem*?), which does not fit Godfrey's teaching that the habit accounts for the intensity of the act. A is followed.","verified")
n("n819","s051-03","quodlibeto. xi q. 4.","la","textual","A prints *xi* and an abbreviation that looks like *q*. B appears to read *quolib. ii. q. 4*. Godfrey of Fontaines's locus has not been verified in either form.","uncertain")
n("n820","s051-03","Est opinio magistri","la","source","Peter Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 17 (charity is the Holy Spirit himself). The view was commonly rejected by the scholastics, hence *a theologis reprobatur*.","certain")
n("n821","s051-04","de moribus ecclesie. c. 4.","la","source","Augustine, *De moribus ecclesiae catholicae* I. The commentary on Rom 8:35 and the phrase *caritas … dei hec dicta est virtus* have not been located; the chapter number 4 is not verified.","to-verify")
n("n822","s051-04","ad Romanos. 4°. Quis vos separabit","la","textual","Rom 8:35. The ‘4’ is an error found in both A and B. B reads *Quis nos separabit* (Vulgate); A reads *vos*.","verified")
n("n823","s051-05","gracia et veritas per Jhesum facta est","la","intertext","Jn 1:17 (*gratia et veritas per Iesum Christum facta est*).","certain")
n("n824","s051-06","de potentia absoluta potest acceptare","la","doctrinal","The characteristic Scotist doctrine of divine *acceptatio*: by his absolute power God could accept someone to eternal life without created charity. Compare Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 17 p. 1 qq. 1–2.","to-verify")
n("n825","s051-05","tunc aliquid inheret","la","textual","The headline of p. 83 already reads *Q.ii*, although q. 1 runs to the middle of the page.","certain")
n("n826","s051-04","that verse of Romans 4","en","translation","The reference is printed *4°*; the verse is Rom 8:35.")
n("n827","s051-07","given is the Holy Spirit","en","translation","Latin *sit spiritus sancti*: either ‘is the Holy Spirit's’ or ‘is [that] of the Holy Spirit’. The contrast with *per spiritum sanctum* requires the possessive.")

# --- B collation (full): B68R–B69R
n("n993","s051-02","Et sic aliqui sunt libri hic corrupti","la","textual","B: *Et sic aliqui libri sunt hic corrupti*.","certain")
n("n994","s051-03","sed hec opinio a theologis","la","textual","B: *Sed opinio a theologis* (om. *hec*).","certain")
n("n995","s051-05","dicitur quod necessarium est ponere","la","textual","B: *quod necessario est ponere* (om. *dicitur*).","certain")
upd("n824", append="B: *deus de potentia sua absoluta potest acceptare*.")
n("n997","s051-07","sit spiritus sancti","la","textual","B: *quod caritas diffusa vel data sit spiritussanctus. sed intelligitur quod sit diffusa* (nominative *spiritus sanctus*; also *sit* for A's *est* in the second clause). B gives exactly the Master's thesis (Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 17: charity is the Holy Spirit), which the reply denies; A's genitive is probably a misprint. A is kept; the translation follows B.","certain")
upd("n827", text="Translated from B's *sit spiritus sanctus*, ‘is the Holy Spirit’ (Lombard's thesis that charity is the Holy Spirit himself). A prints *sit spiritus sancti*, ‘is [that] of the Holy Spirit’, which blurs the contrast with *per spiritum sanctum*. See the Latin note.")
